\caption(Actual failed-test rebuilds on a right triangle.)
\alttext(Immediate circle updates lead to the hypotenuse circle with radius2.5.)

> Retain the original eighty-point cloud

The original generator uses std::mt19937 seed2718281 and normal_distribution
with mean0 and standard deviation2, drawing x then y for eighty points. It now
lives in the native library. The solver's independent processing shuffle uses
MT19937-64 seed42. Standard-library distribution and shuffle implementations can
affect exact coordinates/order across toolchains; the trace retains the actual
values used here.

Equal geometric scales keep the circle circular. Boundary samples are produced
by the native circle helper and saved as a local SVG. No external dataset is
necessary for this geometric kernel.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/circle_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto points = dm::geometry::enclosing_circle_demo();
    auto c = dm::geometry::min_enclosing_circle(points);
    auto check = dm::geometry::enclosing_circle_check(c, points);
    std::vector<double> x, y, cx, cy;
    for (auto q : points) {
        x.push_back(q.x);
        y.push_back(q.y);
    }
    for (auto q : dm::geometry::circle_boundary(c)) {
        cx.push_back(q.x);
        cy.push_back(q.y);
    }
    double span = c.radius * 1.2;
    std::print("| points | center x | center y | radius | outside tolerance | near boundary |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               points.size(), c.center.x, c.center.y, c.radius, check.outside,
               check.near_boundary);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(cx, cy, "native enclosing circle", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(
        x, y, "original cloud", {100, 116, 139}, 5).points({c.center.x},
                                                           {c.center.y},
                                                           "center",
                                                           {37, 99, 235}, 7).size(850, 850).margins(95, 35, 60, 70).x_limits(c.center.x - span, c.center.x + span).y_limits(c.center.y - span, c.center.y + span).title("Original normal cloud: native enclosing circle").x_label("x").y_label("y").save_svg("build/circle_original.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| points | center x | center y | radius | outside tolerance | near boundary |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 80 | 0.10211735975725 | 0.19880033549635634 | 5.93856910178991 | 0 | 2 |
\image(figures/circle_original.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The original eighty points and returned circle, in equal-scale geometry.)
\alttext(The native diagnostics report tolerance-aware outside and near-boundary counts without identifying essential support points.)

> Residuals are more informative than the picture

Define radial residual as distance to the returned center minus returned radius.
Negative values are inside; positive values can be admitted by the containment
tolerance1e−9 times max(1,radius). The next figure and table preserve all eighty
original-order residuals. A point within this tolerance of the boundary is near
it numerically; it need not be an essential determining point.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/circle_residuals.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto points = dm::geometry::enclosing_circle_demo();
    auto t = dm::geometry::min_enclosing_circle_trace(points);
    auto check = dm::geometry::enclosing_circle_check(t.result, points);
    std::vector<double> x;
    std::print("Actual containment tests: {}. Capture units: {}.\n\n| original point ID | signed radial " "residual |\n| ---: | ---: |\n",
               t.events.size(), t.captured_entries);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < check.residuals.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(i);
        std::print("| {} | {:.17g} |\n", i, check.residuals[i]);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, check.residuals, "actual signed residual", {37, 99, 235}, 5).abline_h(0, {220, 38, 38}, 1).legend({"signed residual", "exact boundary residual0"}, {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}}).title("Original cloud: native radial residuals").x_label("original point ID").y_label("distance minus radius").save_svg("build/circle_residuals.svg");
}
```
